  {
    "id": "2069518693139435882",
    "author": "0xclodex",
    "authorName": "Clodex",
    "url": "https://x.com/0xclodex/status/2069518693139435882",
    "text": "Boris Cherny, head of Claude Code:\n\n\"I actually just ran out of hard problems to give it.\"\n\nevery problem he fed the newest model got one-shotted - he couldn't invent a harder one.\n\nand he practices what he preaches: 100% of his code written by AI since Opus 4. ~1,700 PRs this year, 8 billion tokens since March, most of it prompted from his phone.\n\nhis point: coding is no longer the bottleneck. engineers are now bottlenecked on good ideas.\n\n~40-min fireside, free. the head of Claude Code on what's left for humans to do ↓",
    "createdAtISO": "2026-06-23T20:31:20.000Z",
    "date": "2026-06-24",
    "metrics": {
      "likes": 15,
      "reposts": 2,
      "replies": 3,
      "quotes": 1,
      "views": 1858,
      "bookmarks": 16
    },
    "media": [
      {
        "type": "video",
        "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2069517553131556864/vid/avc1/1280x720/_U4Zo503DHKGHA7D.mp4?tag=28"
      }
    ],
    "raw": {
      "id": "2069518693139435882",
      "text": "Boris Cherny, head of Claude Code:\n\n\"I actually just ran out of hard problems to give it.\"\n\nevery problem he fed the newest model got one-shotted - he couldn't invent a harder one.\n\nand he practices what he preaches: 100% of his code written by AI since Opus 4. ~1,700 PRs this year, 8 billion tokens since March, most of it prompted from his phone.\n\nhis point: coding is no longer the bottleneck. engineers are now bottlenecked on good ideas.\n\n~40-min fireside, free. the head of Claude Code on what's left for humans to do ↓",
      "author": {
        "id": "1686744883556474880",
        "name": "Clodex",
        "screenName": "0xClodex",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2054522025314496512/l2XQl34R_normal.jpg",
        "verified": true
      },
      "metrics": {
        "likes": 15,
        "retweets": 2,
        "replies": 3,
        "quotes": 1,
        "views": 1858,
        "bookmarks": 16
      },
      "createdAt": "Tue Jun 23 20:31:20 +0000 2026",
      "createdAtLocal": "2026-06-24 04:31",
      "createdAtISO": "2026-06-23T20:31:20+00:00",
      "media": [
        {
          "type": "video",
          "url": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2069517553131556864/vid/avc1/1280x720/_U4Zo503DHKGHA7D.mp4?tag=28",
          "width": 1280,
          "height": 720
        }
      ],
      "urls": [],
      "isRetweet": false,
      "retweetedBy": null,
      "lang": "en",
      "score": null,
      "quotedTweet": {
        "id": "2069167494661648603",
        "text": "AI builder Ras Mic on the agentic-loops hype:\n\n\"human in the loop is the best loop.\"\n\nin a ~20-min pod he argues that \"fire a loop and walk away\" - the thing top builders keep flexing - is a token-burning trap for anyone not on an unlimited plan.\n\nhis exhibit A: Peter Steinberger's screenshot - $1.3M in tokens in a single month.\n\nthe one place a loop actually works? a tight code-review loop, scored 1–5, that never ships below a 4.\n\nworth more than a $500 vibe-coding course. watch today ↓",
        "author": {
          "screenName": "0xClodex",
          "name": "Clodex"
        }
      }
    },
